<form>
  <label>Frothly intrusion investigation</label>
  <description>Entity-centric view of the BOTS v3 intrusion, enriched with identity and asset lookups. Start here, then drill into a scenario.</description>
  <fieldset submitButton="false">
    <input type="time" token="tr">
      <default>
        <earliest>-10y</earliest>
        <latest>now</latest>
      </default>
    </input>
  </fieldset>
  <row>
    <panel>
      <single>
        <title>Anonymous O365 link retrievals</title>
        <search>
          <query><![CDATA[`frothly_index` eventtype=frothly_o365_management Operation=AnonymousLinkUsed UserId=anonymous | stats dc(ClientIP)]]></query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="colorBy">value</option>
        <option name="rangeColors">["0x53a051","0xdc4e41"]</option>
        <option name="rangeValues">[0]</option>
        <option name="useColors">1</option>
        <drilldown>
          <link target="_blank">search?q=search%20%60frothly_index%60%20eventtype%3Dfrothly_o365_management%20Operation%3DAnonymousLinkUsed%20UserId%3Danonymous&amp;earliest=-10y&amp;latest=now</link>
        </drilldown>
      </single>
    </panel>
    <panel>
      <single>
        <title>Foreign Azure AD sign-ins</title>
        <search>
          <query><![CDATA[`frothly_index` eventtype=frothly_aad_signin loginStatus=Success NOT (location.country=US OR location.country=CA) | stats count]]></query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="colorBy">value</option>
        <option name="rangeColors">["0x53a051","0xdc4e41"]</option>
        <option name="rangeValues">[0]</option>
        <option name="useColors">1</option>
        <drilldown>
          <link target="_blank">search?q=search%20%60frothly_index%60%20eventtype%3Dfrothly_aad_signin%20loginStatus%3DSuccess%20NOT%20%28location.country%3DUS%20OR%20location.country%3DCA%29&amp;earliest=-10y&amp;latest=now</link>
        </drilldown>
      </single>
    </panel>
    <panel>
      <single>
        <title>AWS console logins without MFA</title>
        <search>
          <query><![CDATA[`frothly_index` eventtype=frothly_aws_cloudtrail eventName=ConsoleLogin additionalEventData.MFAUsed=No | stats count]]></query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="colorBy">value</option>
        <option name="rangeColors">["0x53a051","0xdc4e41"]</option>
        <option name="rangeValues">[0]</option>
        <option name="useColors">1</option>
        <drilldown>
          <link target="_blank">search?q=search%20%60frothly_index%60%20eventtype%3Dfrothly_aws_cloudtrail%20eventName%3DConsoleLogin%20additionalEventData.MFAUsed%3DNo&amp;earliest=-10y&amp;latest=now</link>
        </drilldown>
      </single>
    </panel>
  </row>
  <row>
    <panel>
      <table>
        <title>Cloud identities and roles (O365)</title>
        <search>
          <query><![CDATA[`frothly_index` eventtype=frothly_o365_management `frothly_users` | stats count values(Operation) as operations by UserId | lookup frothly_identities identity as UserId OUTPUT role team | sort -count]]></query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="drilldown">row</option>
        <drilldown>
          <link target="_blank">search?q=search%20%60frothly_index%60%20eventtype%3Dfrothly_o365_management%20%60frothly_users%60%20%7C%20stats%20count%20values%28Operation%29%20as%20operations%20by%20UserId%20%7C%20lookup%20frothly_identities%20identity%20as%20UserId%20OUTPUT%20role%20team%20%7C%20sort%20-count&amp;earliest=-10y&amp;latest=now</link>
        </drilldown>
      </table>
    </panel>
    <panel>
      <table>
        <title>Endpoint hosts, owners, and criticality</title>
        <search>
          <query><![CDATA[`frothly_index` eventtype=frothly_wineventlog_security | stats count by host | lookup frothly_assets host OUTPUT owner criticality zone | sort -count]]></query>
          <earliest>$tr.earliest$</earliest>
          <latest>$tr.latest$</latest>
        </search>
        <option name="drilldown">row</option>
        <drilldown>
          <link target="_blank">search?q=search%20%60frothly_index%60%20eventtype%3Dfrothly_wineventlog_security%20%7C%20stats%20count%20by%20host%20%7C%20lookup%20frothly_assets%20host%20OUTPUT%20owner%20criticality%20zone%20%7C%20sort%20-count&amp;earliest=-10y&amp;latest=now</link>
        </drilldown>
      </table>
    </panel>
  </row>
  <row>
    <panel>
      <html>
        <div style="padding:4px 8px">
          <p>One intrusion across six scenarios on 2018-08-20. <b>bstoll</b> ties the cloud-to-endpoint thread (AWS recon, the BSTOLL-L laptop, the Coinhive miner); <b>fyodor</b> ties the PowerShell implant to the Azure AD sign-ins and the O365 mailbox abuse; <b>bgist</b> carries the stolen cloud accounts into the anonymous OneDrive share.</p>
          <p>KPI tiles turn red when a signal is present in the selected window. The tables enrich raw activity with the role and asset context the <code>frothly_identities</code> and <code>frothly_assets</code> lookups carry. Click any panel to pivot to the underlying events.</p>
        </div>
      </html>
    </panel>
  </row>
</form>
